<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:19:17Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Israel votes in first election since October 7 attack as Netanyahu faces crucial test</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:890985c515444434b2a2250295d6fd129016e887e19edaf33986a02e84d92850</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:18:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T04:12:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261027-israel-election-2026-netanyahu-october-7--393517cfbc4c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261027-israel-election-2026-netanyahu-october-7" /><summary type="html">Israelis head to the polls on Tuesday for the first time since Hamas's October 7, 2023 attack, in a closely contested election seen as a referendum on Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu. The vote follows three years of regional wars, with Netanyahu running neck and neck with centrist rival Gadi Eisenkot.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Kylian Mbappe loses two major China sponsorship deals over Mao Zedong joke</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e6f5c866f4ba01f40e0c399af5b67ffec9498b5c0ddfdca0520262a63d65e233</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:18:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T03:54:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/sport/20261027-kylian-mbappe-china-mao-zedong-sponsorship-deal--5dc8293a4ccf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/sport/20261027-kylian-mbappe-china-mao-zedong-sponsorship-deal" /><summary type="html">French football star Kylian Mbappe was dropped by two major Chinese brands on Tuesday after a video circulated online in which he appeared to joke about former leader Mao Zedong. Energy drink giant Dongpeng and dairy producer Mengniu said they had terminated their partnerships, citing remarks that offended Chinese national sentiment.</summary><category term="Sport" /></entry><entry><title>US-EU trade truce at risk over $3.4 billion Airbus loan, Trump official warns</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d2556e68237ea4658ce331bc7869ed9c5c5d33c68c1d7624180501ec23dd0b58</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:18:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T02:20:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261027-us-eu-trade-truce-airbus-loan-trump--677a525d064d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261027-us-eu-trade-truce-airbus-loan-trump" /><summary type="html">US Trade Representative Jamieson Greer warned on Monday that a $3.4 billion European Investment Bank loan to Airbus could jeopardise a tariff truce between Washington and Brussels. Greer said his office had received no details about the financing, announced in June, and urged the EU to resolve the matter quickly.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Flavio Bolsonaro vows to lead opposition after Brazil court imposes travel ban</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a951b8cdb4453bccf9720e406bfa4415282bb5e16bc1ca366a5f52ad4f57a802</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:18:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T23:56:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261026-flavio-bolsonaro-opposition-brazil-court-travel-ban--4575bf06ed5b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261026-flavio-bolsonaro-opposition-brazil-court-travel-ban" /><summary type="html">Brazilian presidential candidate Flavio Bolsonaro said on Monday a Supreme Court justice had barred him from leaving the country after he narrowly lost to incumbent Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva. Bolsonaro, who refused to concede defeat, denounced the order as intimidation and vowed to challenge the election results.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Harry Kane ends England's 25-year Ballon d'Or drought, Putellas wins third crown</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:65f4254f9b8c09e3c9ffddccfe7403ad8a645f1893b9d5bf32643a836a5f1396</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:18:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T23:45:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/sport/20261026-harry-kane-ballon-dor-2026-alexia-putellas--80e55f83cb7c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/sport/20261026-harry-kane-ballon-dor-2026-alexia-putellas" /><summary type="html">Harry Kane became the first Englishman in 25 years to win the Ballon d’Or on Monday after scoring 73 goals for club and country last season. Spain’s Alexia Putellas claimed her third women’s award after helping Barcelona win the Champions League, ending teammate Aitana Bonmati’s three-year reign.</summary><category term="Sport" /></entry><entry><title>Europe's top NATO powers pledge greater defence role, reaffirm US alliance</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:84dc9782a0fc37bef1f748069b031acfeb8990ed3434c21eeeddc99c353cd603</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:18:59Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T23:33:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261026-europe-nato-defence-responsibility-us-alliance--7fa969338f30.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261026-europe-nato-defence-responsibility-us-alliance" /><summary type="html">Europe's five main NATO members said on Monday they were ready to take greater responsibility for the continent's security while reaffirming the United States as an "indispensable ally". Defence ministers from France, Germany, Italy, Poland and Britain pledged closer co-operation with Washington after talks in Paris on strengthening Europe's defence role.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Mecca pact nations hold talks with Iran to prevent renewed Middle East war</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:03c407db9103095a6cffa19a6ae5fe54a053eba7988dc57239272a3193791d1f</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:19:02Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T23:24:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261026-iran-talks-mecca-pact-nations-war--271d84436965.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261026-iran-talks-mecca-pact-nations-war" /><summary type="html">Senior officials from Saudi Arabia, Turkey and Pakistan held talks in Iran on Monday aimed at preventing renewed fighting in the Middle East, with Tehran describing discussions as “very good”. The diplomatic push, attended by Saudi Defence Minister Prince Khalid bin Salman, followed warnings from Washington, Tehran and Israel of renewed hostilities.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Protests in Europe: Fact-checking viral videos amid claims of 'chaos'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3bc5ce378fa912560f4b16539af468e71de8527d63bba96228ab9cb64deb518e</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:19:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T22:18:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261026-protests-in-europe-fact-checking-viral-videos-amid-claims-of-chaos--15058a7a9f55.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261026-protests-in-europe-fact-checking-viral-videos-amid-claims-of-chaos" /><summary type="html">As young people protest poor school conditions and the rising cost of living across Europe, misleading videos are spreading online. Footage from Poland in 2017, military preparations in Portugal and a protest in Argentina have all been falsely presented as recent demonstrations in Europe, painting a misleading picture of unrest. Vedika Bahl fact-checks three viral videos to uncover what they really show and how old footage is recycled to spread misinformation and attract clicks.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>Anthropic's IPO filing shows soaring sales and steep losses</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:694d23c041884b7f7c54406f74e37fc8fa91ec9a2d5904d150453689f7255516</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:19:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T22:01:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20261026-anthropic-s-ipo-filing-shows-soaring-sales-and-steep-losses--dea5ec9dcca1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20261026-anthropic-s-ipo-filing-shows-soaring-sales-and-steep-losses" /><summary type="html">AI giant Anthropic has publicly filed for an initial public offering (IPO) with US market regulators.  The document offered a glimpse into the company's finances but also contained nearly 100 pages related to risks around investing in the company.  The filing revealed that in the first half of 2026, its revenue soared to $16.3 billion while net loss widened to over $80 billion.  Plus, London's iconic Oxford Street, one of Europe's busiest shopping areas, has been partially pedestrianised.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Serbia’s elections: 'Tracking fraud for sure had an impact on the results'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5e6bd69336efeacc6b7d2a316bcbffd46e2e6a8aa9bcd189af79cfadc5865210</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:19:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T21:49:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261026-serbia-elections-tracking-fraud-had-an-impact-on-results-vote-fraud--fc816450d254.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261026-serbia-elections-tracking-fraud-had-an-impact-on-results-vote-fraud" /><summary type="html">On October 25, Serbia's student-led protest movement won a historic victory in parliamentary ⁠elections, defeating outgoing President Aleksandar Vucic's party. Supporters of the student list explained to FRANCE 24 how they mounted a massive mobilisation to fight electoral fraud and monitor the electoral process inside and outside the polling stations.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>The fall of El-Fasher, one year on</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d9c4638157b0b87e90cc92a25db53e6468d79c70fc9124a20013d0d8a5b31203</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:19:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T21:26:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/the-fall-of-el-fasher-one-year-on--b474e4157040.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/the-fall-of-el-fasher-one-year-on" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition, 15 military officials are sanctioned by the UK over the brutality and abuse of civilians during the fall of El Fasher. Also, ⁠Algeria's set to send in army units ​to ‌Niger ⁠to ‌protect energy ⁠and economic interests there. And days after a foreigner was beaten to death on the streets of Durban, the stalled asylum process has left many migrants living in fear.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Trump offers $1 million for tipoffs leading to vote fraud conviction as midterms approach</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:53d1af7b933b04cc5f32672cee6b22fba4a523604e45ced4d073d1a5a2e756bb</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:19:17Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T21:17:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261026-trump-offers-1-million-for-tipoffs-leading-to-vote-fraud-conviction-as-midterms-approach--cb23d5a53a80.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261026-trump-offers-1-million-for-tipoffs-leading-to-vote-fraud-conviction-as-midterms-approach" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump on Monday pledged a $1 million reward for information on voter fraud leading to conviction ahead of the upcoming 2026 US midterms on November 3. The president gave no details of how the reward would be funded or administered. The comments follow his repeated false claims that he won the 2020 presidential election.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Serbian student movement eyes power after election triumph</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9066362ac2b63b8774aef2ed9a2e7e614f24337934cfb97ccfccd00e3272da62</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:17:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T19:48:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/serbian-student-movement-eyes-power-after-election-triumph--396143e74db4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/serbian-student-movement-eyes-power-after-election-triumph" /><summary type="html">Emotions ran high in Belgrade on Monday after a student-led movement upset the right-wing populist Aleksandar Vucic's party in Serbia's snap election. A celebratory mood gripped the capital, with drivers honking their horns and passers-by holding up three fingers -- the winning list's ballot number and a Serbian greeting. Many wore badges and other symbols of the student movement, while a large group of residents spent the day cleaning up a park between parliament and the presidency after Vucic loyalists, who had camped there for more than a year, fled. FRANCE 24's Mark Owen speaks with researchers and political activist Aleksandar Matković.</summary></entry><entry><title>Comeback kid: How did Brazil veteran-leader Lula upset Bolsonaro?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7b16fc5f02763f6614a386104e912f03da865eb2863d4ebe9d3279d6bf3124f2</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:17:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T19:22:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261026-comeback-kid-how-did-brazil-veteran-leader-lula-upset-bolsonaro--c3955199ecd8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261026-comeback-kid-how-did-brazil-veteran-leader-lula-upset-bolsonaro" /><summary type="html">Two days shy of his 81st birthday… Brazil’s Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva emerging as the comeback kid. Coming from behind in the polls after a bitter campaign where he often showed his age, Lula becoming the first candidate since Brazil’s return to democracy in the 1980s to win the presidential runoff after trailing in the first round. How did the Workers Party leader turn a 2-point-2 million vote deficit against the far-right's Flavio Bolsonaro into a 4-point-4 million vote win? Reminder that three short weeks ago, most races at the federal and state level broke the way of conservatives and the far-right?</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>UN cites 'ethnic cleansing' concerns around Israel's Palestinian displacement operation in Hebron</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8926073d072a76020969ce2386ae072e730fd47aff1bb2264fe054a13679f23c</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:17:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T17:59:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261026-un-cites-ethnic-cleansing-concerns-around-israel-palestinian-displacement-operation-hebron--f54dc7b36717.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261026-un-cites-ethnic-cleansing-concerns-around-israel-palestinian-displacement-operation-hebron" /><summary type="html">The United Nations on Monday raised "ethnic cleansing" concerns following Israel's operation to displace by force more than 3,000 Palestinians from their homes in Hebron in the West Bank after two Palestinian gunmen killed two Israeli soldiers at a checkpoint near the city on Friday. UN rights chief Volker Turk said in a statement that the "aggressive operation" must end, and that "collective punishment is a grave violation of international law".</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>French student union leaders call for 'continued mobilisation' after meeting PM</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e0fb53de88269c701460939d8449546e91efacfb6ab308dc796ed63fbe9c6912</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:17:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T17:37:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261026-french-student-union-leaders-call-for-continued-mobilisation-after-meeting-pm--c60adecb5ed9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261026-french-student-union-leaders-call-for-continued-mobilisation-after-meeting-pm" /><summary type="html">The French government met student representatives on Monday (October 26) following weeks of unrest. Students who had been demanding a meeting for weeks hail progress. Nonetheless they are now calling for fresh demonstrations next Saturday (October 31) to press for further measures. Details by FRANCE 24’s French Politics Editor Marc Perelman.</summary></entry><entry><title>Brazil: What does Lula's re-election mean for the Amazon?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c7e0874ab476ac6b76ae904917c69618f793eed93a91522c2015f8b5359b0c2b</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:17:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T17:18:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/brazil-what-does-lula-s-re-election-mean-for-the-amazon--6f4fc14c1029.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/brazil-what-does-lula-s-re-election-mean-for-the-amazon" /><summary type="html">Climate activists in Brazil are celebrating President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva's election victory as good news for the Amazon rainforest. His last four years in power saw a record decrease in deforestation in the world's largest rainforest.</summary></entry><entry><title>Opponents accuse Netanyahu of stoking tensions with Iran before Israel's election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:caa04d649c46961eadfb64f1e345f13682d6553a54da3f12a685d6ba3326f336</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:17:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T17:11:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/opponents-accuse-netanyahu-of-stoking-tensions-with-iran-before-israel-s-election--5429441497ca.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/opponents-accuse-netanyahu-of-stoking-tensions-with-iran-before-israel-s-election" /><summary type="html">Israel's defence minister denied on Monday (October 26) reports of a rift between PM Netanyahu and the army over Iran, before the vote.  Netanyahu has campaigned heavily on his security credentials, insisting only he can "finish the job" in the US-Israeli war on Iran. His main rival, ex-army chief Gadi Eisenkot, has accused him of playing up the Iran threat when it suits him politically, and of failing to accomplish his war goals. FRANCE 24's Kethevane Gorjestani tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Leaders across Americas react to Brazil President Lula's re-election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:70782ff0e2a4c802493cfef51f38647552cc41933afda2fea3597824fb302900</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:17:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T17:05:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/leaders-across-americas-react-to-brazil-president-lula-s-re-election--efc0688d3f0e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/leaders-across-americas-react-to-brazil-president-lula-s-re-election" /><summary type="html">​President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva won Brazil's presidential election on Sunday (October 25), defeating right-wing ​Senator Flavio Bolsonaro in a runoff to secure a fourth non-consecutive term.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israeli candidate Eisenkot pledges to unite country as Netanyahu deems him 'soft' on Iran</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5379cf9d26cf1a130a5086d0fbb9b6725b512dc224491208eef87b5079f049b1</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:17:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T16:58:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261026-israeli-candidate-eisenkot-pledges-to-unite-israelis-as-netanyahu-deems-him-soft-on-iran--bd8634a89185.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261026-israeli-candidate-eisenkot-pledges-to-unite-israelis-as-netanyahu-deems-him-soft-on-iran" /><summary type="html">Israeli presidential candidate Gadi Eisenkot's pledge made Sunday to "heal" Israeli society after Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's divisive tenure resonated with some voters attending his final campaign rally before polling begins Tuesday. Netanyahu meanwhile received fresh backing for re-election from US President Donald Trump and deemed Eisenkot "soft" on Iran.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>'Lula accustomed to negotiating tough bargains': Campaign promises collide with right-wing Congress</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aec37b397da1d0b97af927392fd9932f046fd32879e262712c1c9c3a65f35361</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:17:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T16:54:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/lula-accustomed-to-negotiating-tough-bargains-campaign-promises-collide-with-right-wing-congress--662d1f784eef.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/lula-accustomed-to-negotiating-tough-bargains-campaign-promises-collide-with-right-wing-congress" /><summary type="html">Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Christopher Sabatini, Director of Chatham House's Latin America Programme. Sabatini examines how Lula's campaign reinvention, youth mobilisation, and the changing dynamics of Bolsonarismo are reshaping Brazil's political landscape. By embracing social media, mobilising younger voters, and shifting attention from his historical achievements to the economic anxieties of ordinary Brazilians, Lula managed to transform the electoral contest. As Sabatini explains, voters were no longer satisfied with hearing about the past. They wanted an answer to a more immediate question: "What are you going to do for us now?</summary></entry><entry><title>Israel election: unable to vote from abroad, expats have to fly home</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c9a581091813ca92dfd653490de3594abe24db8330fe83cb035b1e4cde830661</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:17:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T16:47:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/israel-election-unable-to-vote-from-abroad-expats-have-to-fly-home--cdb70f36234d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/israel-election-unable-to-vote-from-abroad-expats-have-to-fly-home" /><summary type="html">Israelis can’t vote from abroad, so tens of thousands of expats are expected to fly home for the election. At Tel Aviv airport, supporters of opposition figure Gadi Eisenkot are already waiting at arrivals. A “Fly and Vote” initiative helps expats organise their trip, despite a failed petition from Netanyahu’s Likud party to restrict it. With polls predicting a tight race, every vote could count, and the result will decide the Prime Minister’s fate.</summary></entry><entry><title>Macklemore holds charity stadium shows to raise funds for Palestine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d8ae061cbffe5217eee434bfd5933ef96b425f680ca0edf258ef9077bee2c0f8</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:17:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T16:26:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261026-macklemore-holds-charity-stadium-shows-to-raise-funds-for-palestine--cd369e23887b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261026-macklemore-holds-charity-stadium-shows-to-raise-funds-for-palestine" /><summary type="html">In this arts24 music show, Jennifer Ben Brahim brings us a roundup of the big music releases and news of the week, from US rapper Macklemore's charity stadium shows to raise money for Palestine, to the return of R'n'B crooner John Legend with his 11th album "Muse" – his first collaboration with close friend Pharrell Williams.</summary><category term="arts24" /></entry><entry><title>France protests: Macron rules out state of emergency – for now</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e3120878f93258fab2cf5705e3c0bb32b73144ed02f450e8af2822257fae6915</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:17:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T16:16:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261026-france-protests-macron-rules-out-state-of-emergency-_-for-now--d78e2f54223a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261026-france-protests-macron-rules-out-state-of-emergency-%E2%80%93-for-now" /><summary type="html">The French government sought to draw a line Monday under weeks of protests that have been marred by violence, with President Emmanuel Macron heading to Marseille. France has been rocked by widespread anger over the rising cost of living, with nationwide demonstrations on October 17 degenerating into some of the country's worst rioting in years.</summary></entry></feed>
